description:
Write `long long power(long long base, int exponent)` recursively, for `exponent >= 0`.

Multiplying `base` by itself `exponent` times works but is slow. A better idea halves the problem each time:

- anything to the power 0 is 1;
- for an even exponent, `base^n = (base^(n/2))²`;
- for an odd exponent, the same times one more `base`.

That needs about 30 steps for an exponent of a billion instead of a billion steps.

starter.solution.cpp:
long long power(long long base, int exponent)
{
    return 0;
}

solution.solution.cpp:
long long power(long long base, int exponent)
{
    if (exponent == 0)
    {
        return 1;
    }
    const long long half{ power(base, exponent / 2) };
    if (exponent % 2 == 0)
    {
        return half * half;
    }
    return half * half * base;
}

unitTests:
TEST("small powers") { CHECK_EQ(power(2, 10), 1024); CHECK_EQ(power(3, 4), 81); CHECK_EQ(power(5, 1), 5); }
TEST("power of zero") { CHECK_EQ(power(7, 0), 1); CHECK_EQ(power(0, 0), 1); }
TEST("negative base") { CHECK_EQ(power(-2, 3), -8); CHECK_EQ(power(-2, 4), 16); }
TEST("large") { CHECK_EQ(power(2, 62), 4611686018427387904LL); CHECK_EQ(power(1, 1000000000), 1); }

